{"diagnosis": "Loopback with divider 64 sent 0xa5 but recv_buf_data returned 0xe0 causing TRAP: uart data mismatch got 0xe0 want 0xa5 and tohost FAIL 0xdead. CONE_SLICE picosoc/picosoc.v:120-121 and picosoc/simpleuart.v:20 confirm divider path, agreeing with trace divider 64. Root cause in excerpt at lines 90 and 97: states 10/default compare recv_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4) instead of > cfg_divider, sampling each bit 16x too fast and corrupting recv_pattern into recv_buf_data.", "patch_diff": "diff --git a/picosoc/simpleuart.v b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
--- a/picosoc/simpleuart.v
+++ b/picosoc/simpleuart.v
@@ -89,13 +89,13 @@
 				10: begin
-					if (recv_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4)) begin
+					if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
 						recv_buf_data <= recv_pattern;
 						recv_buf_valid <= 1;
 						recv_state <= 0;
 					end
 				end
 				default: begin
-					if (recv_divcnt > (cfg_divider >> 4)) begin
+					if (recv_divcnt > cfg_divider) begin
 						recv_pattern <= {ser_rx, recv_pattern[7:1]};
 						recv_state <= recv_state + 1;
 						recv_divcnt <= 0;
", "expected": "tohost PASS, no TRAP uart data mismatch, loopback 0xa5 received correctly, checksum != 27ee482b473c74db5dce8b5ab1a233084cce3055c317a1f2045faa6dbc13a1c6"}

